I am honored to receive the award for winning picture in animal portraits for this picture of a bonobo with a young mongoose from @naturein_focus! Thanks so much to the jury… I am delighted!

This is an amazing opportunity to inform more people know about bonobos, their behavior and how threatened they are in the wild! This image was only possible by working closely with Barbara Fruth and her excellent research team at the Max-Planck Institute for Animals Behavior in Konstanz and the LuiKotale Bonobo Project in Democratic Republic of Congo. 

I’m sorry that I didn’t respond sooner. I’m on vacation with my family in France… and trying very hard to stay offline for a few weeks - we all need some offline time 😊

More posts about bonobos when I’m back from vacation…

